When working on UI code, always use the project design system context:

- @docs/design-system/Symphonica_design.md
- @docs/design-system/design_tokens.json (including **`meta.llmImplementationNotes.cardHeaderFiltersImplementationContract`** for Filters headers, **`cardHeaderStickyImplementationContract`** / **`primaryCardHeaderStickyScroll`** for sticky scroll, and **`symphonicaBootstrapFormAccents`** / **§5.12** for Bootstrap form accents)

**Primary Card header — sticky scroll (all variants):** Implement against **§5.5 → Sticky scroll — implementation contract (assistants / Cursor)** in `Symphonica_design.md`. Section header card (header-only `<article>`): **`sym-card-primary sym-card-primary--section-sticky sym-no-hover`** — canonical markup in **`SymphonicaShowcase.tsx`** (pills) and **`PartyDomainShowcase.tsx`** (filters). CSS: **`.sym-card-primary.sym-card-primary--section-sticky`** in `symphonica.css` only. App shell: **`sym-app-main`** **`overflow: visible`** + **`sym-app-body`** **`overflow-y: auto`** (`App.tsx`). **Never:** viewport **`fixed`** on card headers; **`overflow: hidden`** on `sym-app-main`; negative **`margin-bottom`** to cancel `sym-page` gap; extra **`box-shadow`** under sticky (ghost card). Table/data in a **sibling** `<article>`, not inside the sticky header card.

**Primary Card header — Filters (`Simple` / `Advanced`):** Implement against **§5.5 → Filters variant — implementation contract (assistants / Cursor)** in `Symphonica_design.md`. The canonical working markup lives in **`symphonica-ui/src/showcase/PartyDomainShowcase.tsx`** (`sym-card-header` block). Guía reference: [Figma 7872:9277](https://www.figma.com/design/7JdlMVI0UphCTyuHFF9Fww/Guia-de-Estilos-de-Symphonica?node-id=7872-9277). Do not invent alternate header layouts; reuse **`symphonica-ui/src/styles/symphonica.css`** classes (`sym-card-header__*`, `sym-card-header__filter-field--primary-toolbar`, `--advanced-toolbar`, `sym-btn-filled-primary--icon-only` for active **`tune`**). Apply **`sym-card-primary--section-sticky`** on the parent `<article>` per sticky contract above.

This is a React application using Bootstrap (or React-Bootstrap) as the structural foundation for Symphonica.

Rules:
- Preserve existing React functional patterns and hooks logic.
- Do not rewrite complete screens or large component trees unless explicitly requested.
- Do not introduce new dependencies (libraries) unless explicitly requested.
- Do not introduce new visual styles (CSS/inline-styles) unless explicitly requested.

- Bootstrap is part of the foundation of this design system.
- Reuse Bootstrap utilities and layout structure (Rows, Cols, Containers) whenever possible.
- Extend Bootstrap using Symphonica guidelines and tokens.
- Do not replace Bootstrap with another UI framework (like Tailwind or Material UI).

- Symphonica styles and tokens take precedence over default Bootstrap styles.
- When a Bootstrap style conflicts with Symphonica, follow Symphonica.
- Prefer Symphonica visual rules for typography, spacing, colors, borders, shadows and component behavior.

- Use Symphonica tokens instead of hardcoded CSS values.
- If using CSS-in-JS or Styled Components, map props strictly to @docs/design-system/design_tokens.json
- For icons, strictly follow the Material Icons Outlined mapping defined in @Symphonica_design.md.